Claude responded: Since all the graph's structure is encoded in the data file, the cleanest deep copy is simply reloading from it — this guarantees all nodes are freshly allocat…
cpp
// Overloaded assignment operator — creates a deep copy of the rhs graph
const Graph & Graph::operator=(const Graph & rhs) {
    // Self-assignment check
        if (this == &rhs) return *this;

    // Clear existing graph
        clearGraph();

    // Copy member variables
        m_numNodes = rhs.m_numNodes;
	    m_dataFile = rhs.m_dataFile;

    // Rebuild the graph from the same data file
        loadData();

    return *this;
    }
    Since all the graph's structure is encoded in the data file, the cleanest deep copy is simply reloading from it — this guarantees all nodes are freshly allocated and properly wired up without having to manually traverse and duplicate every pointer relationship. Ready for the next one!

