8:52 PM
Claude responded: Great to hear!
Great to hear! A few things come to mind:

Regarding findPath

What happens if findPath is called on a graph with only one node and no connections? It should still handle that gracefully, though it likely already does given our edge case test.
Regarding operator=

Self-assignment is handled with the if (this == &rhs) check, but what if m_dataFile is empty on the right hand side? Since our implementation relies on loadData() to rebuild the graph, an empty filename would cause loadData() to fail silently and produce an empty graph rather than a true copy.
Regarding clearGraph()

Since the destructor relies on it, if clearGraph() ever fails to properly null m_head, the destructor could potentially cause undefined behavior on subsequent calls.
Regarding insert()

If the same node value appears multiple times in the data file, the existing node gets its connections updated rather than duplicated. This is intentional, but could produce unexpected results if the data file is malformed.
General

There's no validation on node values — negative values other than -1 could theoretically be inserted as real nodes, which could cause confusion with the -1 sentinel value.
The operator= empty filename issue is probably the most concerning of these. Would you like to address any of them?

